A2560Me LAN9221 MiNTNet driver (GPL-2.0-or-later)

Build target: 68EC060, -mshort -msoft-float. Driver entry is common ../main.c.
PIO with a 10 ms root timeout; chip IRQs remain disabled. All hardware polling
loops have finite limits. MAC comes from the build-84+ shared I2C transaction
controller's factory EEPROM, or a valid already-programmed LAN9221 address.
Attach requires the A2560Me FVRM cookie and chip ID to avoid probing other boards.
The interface is named enN, normally en0. Bring up/down through ifconfig.

Register facts: Microchip LAN9221 DS00002416A, A2560Me hardware reference rev1.8.
The board swaps 32-bit register byte lanes. board.h centralizes that conversion;
hw.c packs FIFO words explicitly so packet bytes and final padding are portable.
No byte-sized LAN accesses are used. Do not reset the shared I2C controller.

Runtime: INET4.XDD and LAN9221.XIF go in the kernel's module directory, normally
C:/MINT/1-19-CUR, with XDD_LOAD=YES. DHCP uses /dev/bpf. MiNTNet's bpf_write must
preserve Ethernet-II types (IPv4 0x0800), classifying only values <1536 as lengths.
The associated BPF correction is included in this FreeMiNT source tree.

The system workspace supplies DHCP, network utilities, recovery settings, native
LANPROBE.TOS, and host regression tests for the actual core and BPF expression.
